# remember — success
#
# REMEMBER exists only in the childhood-reminescence phase, so this test is the one that must NOT
# pass --skip-childhood: that flag skips the phase entirely and fills the starting kit as if it had
# run. Every other script in the suite passes it, which is why this verb had no test.
#
# The childhood is remembered from the place the protagonist will get up from, through the one
# element that answers a click there: "Myself", which holds the fragments of the memory at hand as a
# container holds its contents. A fragment is looked at, thought about, and reached for.
#
# The phase auto-succeeds by design — no plausibility check, no noetic cost, difficulty 0, so no
# dice. There is no `strategy` here and no meaningful failure case; `cli/remember/` has one script,
# deliberately. The fragment is named: --seed 42 fixes which memory comes first and what it holds.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue

# The phase opens on its own — no travel, no location. Wait for the mode rather than for idleness.
wait mode ChildhoodReminescence 60
advance 12 180
regions

# Nothing around the body answers; the memory's fragments hang from "Myself".
expect Under the Tree
expect-state trees "Myself"
expect-state symbols x3 (disabled)
expect-state symbols a scream

click observe "a scream"
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
click think "a scream"
choose childhood_reminescence
advance 12 180
regions

click act 0
choose 0
advance 12 180

# No dice: the result is up at once.
expect SUCCESS
expect-verb remember

# Its CONTINUE moves on to the next memory, whose fragments take the first one's place under
# "Myself" — and the branch just remembered stays.
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-no-state symbols "a scream"
expect-state symbols manure smelt
expect-state trees "a scream"
expect-state trees "state=done verb=remember"
quit
